<section class="panel"><h3>How accuracy changes</h3><div class="training-steps"><p><strong>1.</strong> You upload a valid CSV and begin retraining.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> The software excludes cancelled/diverted flights and flights without a known arrival delay, then samples up to 50,000 rows.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> For each prediction stage, each model learns from 80% of eligible sampled records and is evaluated on a held-out 20%.</p><p><strong>4.</strong> Accuracy, precision, recall, F1, ROC AUC, confusion matrices and graphs are recalculated. The trained models are saved for predictions.</p></div><p class="field-hint">More rows do not necessarily mean better accuracy. Training data quality, sampling, class imbalance and changes over time matter. Before-departure prediction uses scheduled features only. The separate after-departure models use measured departure delay, which is never available for a future scheduled flight.</p></section>
